@startuml

title Color selection, join, and game start

participant Client1
participant Server
participant Client2

group first player reserves a color and joins
Client1->Server: ChooseColorRequest(BLUE)

alt color is available
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.Snapshot(color reserved, snapshot)

Client1->Server: JoinGameRequest
alt game still has space
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.Snapshot(Player joined, snapshot)
else game became full before the join
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.Err(GAME_FULL)
end
else game does not exist
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.Err(GAME_NOT_FOUND)
else game already started
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult.Err(COLOR_SELECTION_CLOSED)
end
end

group second player selects a color
Client2->Server: ChooseColorRequest(BLUE)
Server-->Client2: GameOperationResult.Err(COLOR_ALREADY_TAKEN)

Client2->Server: ChooseColorRequest(RED)
Server-->Client2: GameOperationResult.Snapshot(color reserved, snapshot)
end

group last player joins
Client2->Server: JoinGameRequest
Server->Server: create players and start game
Server-->Client1: GameViewUpdate(game starts)
Server-->Client2: GameOperationResult.Snapshot(game starts, snapshot)
end

note over Client1, Client2
The client reserves a color before sending JoinGameRequest (GUI version).
end note

@enduml
